    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA rare and luxurious coastal residence occupying a prime position in the heart of Skerries, one of north county Dublin's most sought-after seaside towns. Recently built and extending to approximately 280 sq. M / 3,014 sq. Ft., the property combines classical elegance, bespoke craftsmanship and modern efficiency in a highly convenient setting just moments from the harbour, beaches, schools, cafés and restaurants.\n\n5 Strand Street occupies an exceptional position close to the junction of Strand Street and Harbour Road, placing the very best of Skerries within immediate reach. Presented in turnkey condition and offered fully furnished, 5 Strand Street provides beautifully appointed accommodation with four en-suite bedrooms, sea views, private off-street parking, an EV charging point and an array of high-quality finishes throughout. With an A2 energy rating, underfloor heating, an air source heat pump and high-performance glazing, the house offers an excellent balance of style, comfort and modern convenience.\n\nThe property is approached from Strand Street, where the refined exterior gives way to an impressive and light-filled interior. To the rear, the house opens onto a private landscaped courtyard garden, beyond which there is gated access to private off-street parking with an EV charging point. The overall arrangement provides a rare combination of town-centre convenience, privacy and coastal amenity.\nThe property is a superb example of a recently built coastal home, designed with an emphasis on space, light and craftsmanship. Internally, the accommodation is particularly bright and inviting, with generous proportions, high ceilings and carefully selected finishes creating a strong sense of quality throughout.\nA large entrance hall forms an impressive introduction to the property, featuring a striking double-height staircase, feature chandelier and bespoke panelling and architraves. From here, the principal reception rooms are accessed, including a separate front-facing living room with bespoke media unit, integrated storage and fireplace.\nTo the rear lies the heart of the home, comprising a substantial open-plan kitchen, dining and entertaining area. Designed for both everyday living and formal entertaining, this space includes bespoke kitchen units, a central island, quartz worktops and splashbacks by Brennan Kitchens of Reaghstown, Co. Louth, together with high-specification integrated appliances. A walk-in pantry, plant room and separate dining and seating areas further enhance the functionality of the space.\nNatural light is a defining feature, with three skylights and large sliding doors drawing light into the room and creating a seamless connection with the rear garden. A combination of chandeliers, spotlights and wired lamps provides atmospheric lighting, allowing the space to transition comfortably from daytime family use to evening entertaining. The ground floor also includes a dedicated office, ideal for remote working or study, and the house benefits throughout from underfloor heating, an air source heat pump and high-performance double glazing.\n\nAt first floor level, there are four generous double bedrooms, each with its own luxurious en-suite bathroom and custom-built wardrobes. The principal bedroom enjoys spectacular views across South Strand and the Irish Sea, providing an exceptional coastal outlook. A beautifully finished attic room is accessed via an electronic retractable stairs and offers further flexibility as a second living area, studio, hobby room or additional home office. This space also enjoys sea views, adding further appeal to the upper floor accommodation.\n\nGARDEN AND PARKING\nTo the rear, the landscaped courtyard garden has been designed for ease of maintenance and outdoor enjoyment. It features a combination of gravel and paving, timber cladding, integrated lighting and a private, sheltered character well suited to outdoor dining and relaxation.\nA gated access leads to a private off-street parking area with an EV charging point, a particularly valuable feature in such a central coastal location. A second outdoor patio area lies to the side of the property, with convenient side access to Sandybanks Lane.\n\nLOCATION\n5 Strand Street is situated in the heart of Skerries, a vibrant and highly regarded seaside town on the North County Dublin coast. The property enjoys an outstanding location beside the intersection of Strand Street and Harbour Road, with immediate access to the town centre, harbour and coastline.\nSkerries is renowned for its attractive coastal setting, sandy beaches, harbour, sailing and sea-swimming amenities, as well as its excellent selection of artisan cafés, acclaimed restaurants, independent shops and lively bars. South Strand is accessible directly to the rear, while North Strand and Skerries Harbour are just around the corner.\n\nThe town also offers a strong range of schools, sports clubs and local services, making it a highly desirable location for both family living and those seeking a coastal lifestyle within easy reach of Dublin. The combination of sea views, town-centre convenience and immediate access to the beach makes 5 Strand Street a rare and distinctive offering in one of Skerries' most desirable addresses."
      },
